---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro'
import {
	IS_DRAFT,
	OPERATOR,
	TERMS_DATE_LABEL,
	TERMS_VERSION,
	VENUE,
	field,
} from '../../legal'

/**
 * Английская политика конфиденциальности.
 *
 * Текст — дословный перевод, присланный юристом заказчика 30.07.2026, а не машинный:
 * правки по существу вносятся сразу в обе версии, иначе документы разъедутся.
 * Реквизиты и версия общие с русской страницей и приходят из `legal.ts`.
 */
---

<Page
	title="Privacy Policy — Between Bubbles"
	description="What data Between Bubbles collects, where it is stored, and how to control it."
	noindex={IS_DRAFT}
	longform
	lang="en"
	alternatePath="/privacy"
>
	<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<p class="version">Last updated: {TERMS_DATE_LABEL.en} · Version: {TERMS_VERSION}</p>

	{
		IS_DRAFT && (
			<div class="notice">
				<p style="margin: 0">
					<strong>Draft.</strong> The data inventory, retention periods and the list of
					processors describe the implementation and are accurate. The operator's details
					have not been confirmed yet and are shown in square brackets; until they are
					filled in and the text is reviewed by a lawyer, this document has no legal force.
				</p>
			</div>
		)
	}

	<h2>1. Who Processes the Data</h2>
	<p>
		The Data Controller is {field(OPERATOR.name.en, 'operator name')}
		{' '}(Tax ID {field(OPERATOR.registration, 'operator tax id')}), registered at:
		{' '}{field(OPERATOR.address.en, 'operator address')}. Inquiries regarding any data-related
		matters are accepted via email at:
		{' '}<a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{field(OPERATOR.email, 'contact email address')}</a>.
		Data processing is conducted in accordance with the legislation of
		{' '}{field(VENUE.jurisdiction.en, 'governing law country')}.
	</p>
	<p>
		The legal basis for processing is the performance of the contract you enter into by
		accepting the Terms of Service, and your consent, recorded during registration along
		with the date and document version. Consent can be withdrawn by deleting your account.
	</p>

	<h2>2. What Data is Collected</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Account data:</strong> email address, password hash (argon2id algorithm — the
			password itself is not stored and cannot be recovered), name (if you provided one),
			and date of birth. The date of birth is requested to confirm your legal drinking age
			in accordance with the service rules and is not visible to anyone but you.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Settings:</strong> interface language, theme, timezone, default currency, and
			the toggle for displaying expenses.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Diary content:</strong> tasting entries including date, volume, rating, taste
			characteristics, aromas, and notes; wine cards; price, currency, country of purchase,
			and selected store; photos of the bottle and label.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Technical session data:</strong> IP address and browser string (User-Agent) at
			the time of login. These are necessary to distinguish devices, revoke sessions, and
			rate-limit requests during password entry attempts.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The service does not collect data about your health, does not build advertising profiles,
		and does not enrich your profile with data from external sources.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Photos</h2>
	<p>
		Before saving, the server strips all metadata from the image, including GPS shooting
		coordinates; only the image orientation is retained. Files are stored in a private
		storage bucket and are served via signed URLs with a 5-minute lifespan — unauthorized
		persons cannot access anything via a direct file link.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Who Can See Your Entries</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			By default — only you. There is no global feed, subscriptions, comments, or access for
			other users to view someone else's diaries within the service.
		</li>
		<li>
			A single entry can be published via a shared link. The publication includes photos,
			the wine and its characteristics, rating, taste category, impressions, and notes; your
			name is included only if you have enabled the corresponding toggle. Price, store,
			email address, and your other entries are not included. The link can be revoked in
			one click.
		</li>
		<li>
			Store names form a shared directory available to all users when selecting a store.
			Information about who added the name is not displayed in the interface, and when an
			account is deleted, this link is also erased from the database.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>5. Cookies and Browser Storage</h2>
	<p>
		The service uses one technical cookie — <code>between_bubbles_refresh</code>. It is
		httpOnly (inaccessible to page scripts), transmitted exclusively over HTTPS, restricted
		to the <code>/api/auth</code> path, and lives for 30 days; it contains the session
		extension token. Login is impossible without it, therefore no cookie consent banner is
		required.
	</p>
	<p>
		In the browser's local storage, the service keeps only internal login and logout flags to
		synchronize open tabs. There are no analytical, advertising, or tracking scripts used in
		the service.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Where Data is Stored and Who Else Sees It</h2>
	<p>Data is hosted in a data center located in Frankfurt (Germany). Subcontractors:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>DigitalOcean</strong> — application servers, database, and storage for photos
			and backups.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of service emails: email address confirmation,
			password recovery, and notifications regarding changes in terms. Only the recipient's
			address and the email text are transmitted.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Cloudflare</strong> — domain DNS. User traffic does not pass through
			Cloudflare.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		<strong>Cross-Border Data Transfer.</strong> Because our servers are located in Frankfurt,
		Germany, your data is transferred to and stored within the European Union. Germany provides
		an adequate level of personal data protection in accordance with the GDPR and Georgian data
		protection laws. By agreeing to this Policy, you explicitly consent to such cross-border
		transfer, storage, and processing of your data.
	</p>
	<p>
		Data is not transferred or sold to third parties. The only exception is a lawful request
		from an authorized state body, provided it is presented in the manner prescribed by law.
	</p>

	<h2>7. How Long Data is Stored</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Diary content — as long as the account exists.</li>
		<li>Deleted entries remain in the trash for 30 days, after which they are deleted automatically.</li>
		<li>
			After deletion, an account is kept for 30 days — this serves as a grace period for
			recovery upon request. After this period, entries, wines, photos (including files in
			storage), and personal data are permanently deleted without the possibility of
			recovery.
		</li>
		<li>
			Sessions live for up to 90 days, and information about completed sessions is deleted
			within 7 days after they end.
		</li>
		<li>
			Database backups are kept for up to 30 days; therefore, deleted data completely
			disappears from backups within this timeframe.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>View and correct.</strong> All data about you is visible in the application:
			profile, entries, and photos. They can be modified or deleted at any time.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Export.</strong> Settings → export diary to CSV and JSON formats, without
			contacting support and without waiting.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Delete.</strong> Settings → account deletion. No separate request to support
			is required.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Contact.</strong> Questions, complaints, and requests regarding data
			processing should be directed to
			{' '}<a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{field(OPERATOR.email, 'contact email address')}</a>.
			We will respond within 30 days.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>9. Security</h2>
	<p>
		The connection to the service is secured via HTTPS. Passwords are stored exclusively as
		an argon2id hash, and email links as a token hash with a limited lifespan (one hour for
		password recovery, 24 hours for email confirmation). Changing the password and deleting
		the account will revoke all active sessions. The frequency of login attempts and file
		uploads is rate-limited. Photos reside in closed storage and are accessible only via
		short-lived signed links.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Children</h2>
	<p>
		The service is not intended for individuals under 18 years of age and does not
		intentionally collect their data. If such an account is discovered, it will be
		immediately deleted.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Policy Changes</h2>
	<p>
		New versions are published on this page with an updated date and version number. We will
		notify you of any significant changes via the email address provided during registration.
	</p>
</Page>
